-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- sets: Hedberg's theorem
-- a type with decidable equality is a set (agda/cubical's Discrete→isSet, through stability of
-- its paths: a constant endofunction on each path type)
isSet : {l : Level} → Type l → Type l
isSet A = (a b : A) → (p q : a ≡ b) → p ≡ q
